// endpoint_accept_handed_workspace.proto — AcceptHandedWorkspace: an OLDER
// daemon tells the NEWEST daemon of its state root that it is about to move
// a workspace there (docs/investigations/2026-11-16-several-daemons-plan.md,
// phase 3).
//
// Several daemons may serve one state root at once: the newest holds the
// boot claim, and each older one keeps the workspaces that were busy at its
// handover until each is free to move. A workspace freed on an older daemon
// moves straight to the newest, read from daemon.addr at each move, never
// through every generation in turn. The newest was never told of it in a
// handover manifest, so the older daemon announces the one workspace here,
// and only then transfers it exactly as it transfers one to its own
// successor: the newest arms its adoption rendezvous for the workspace, and
// adopts it once the older daemon releases its serving row.

